#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:2 1a3913d7e8a945199f0fe8cf7224c18b
msgid "Profiles and presets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:4 d9798a50af664043996bdc1b4a342445
msgid ""
"Two words for two different things, and the difference matters because "
"one of them you can change and the other you cannot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:7 372bb682c1dc49e3a939679285e18698
msgid ""
"A **profile** is a vendor's catalogue: which libraries IBM makes, which "
"drives each of those models takes, which cartridges each drive writes. It"
" describes hardware that exists, it ships with the console, and nothing "
"can edit it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:11 2bfe303c6de64ba4b5c27f4361c610ce
msgid ""
"A **preset** is a configuration *you* built from a profile and gave a "
"name to, so you can build that library again without retyping it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:14 53c73ef5e3c144fa8837e996bd9ba598
msgid ""
"Both are templates. Neither is ever a library until you create one from "
"it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:21 e179dc45ce0d4bd9bba17d09ee63f5d4
msgid "The nine profiles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:29 9321f74b81d644ed88fc7872222d49fd
msgid ""
"``mhvtl profile show IBM`` prints the whole catalogue: every library "
"model with its drive and slot limits, and every drive model with the "
"densities it writes and the ones it can only read. It is long, because "
"the real catalogue is long - thirteen library models and twenty drives "
"for IBM alone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:34 345e31e1905e4c99a19382839dacd78f
msgid "The useful column is **WRITES**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:45 de576548ced644618fd10efe7fa7a896
msgid ""
"A profile has no write verbs at all - no ``profile set``, no ``profile "
"delete``. There is nothing to edit: if a drive is not in the list, the "
"vendor does not make it, and making one up would produce a library that "
"identifies itself as hardware that does not exist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:52 5d0ed498b89e404eb6406e4522f0e3d5
msgid ""
"**A vendor's default is not its newest.** IBM's default drive is the "
"ULT3580-TD8, which writes LTO8, while its catalogue reaches the "
"ULT3580-TDA and LTO10. Quantum's default is an SDLT600, which is not LTO "
"at all. So ``mhvtl library create --profile QUANTUM`` on its own builds "
"an SDLT library - correct, and probably not what you wanted. Naming the "
"drive and the density is what pins a library to the newest generation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:60 7d0ca9b9958743e2ae85e470e5152b13
msgid "What a preset is for"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:62 89d17695350e4e74a8dff9e6c111730c
msgid "This is a complete, working command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:70 acad2653ae804b0c98a0365041d3a08d
msgid ""
"Typing it twice is how the second library ends up subtly different from "
"the first. Name it once and it becomes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:78 aa18503d88fc47799ba4661f6361cda1
msgid "Eleven are installed with the console"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:80 4f73b6025ad243738156bbb63987a192
msgid ""
"``/etc/mhvtl-gui/presets.toml.example`` ships one library for every "
"vendor, at the newest cartridge that vendor's drives can write. Copy a "
"table out of it into ``presets.toml`` beside it, or just read it to see "
"what the keys look like."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:103
#: 1ae61d1c9dd94cd6bbf9fb6b4af9cd39
msgid ""
"Three of those are worth a glance, because they are the ones that are not"
" the obvious row. **hp-latest** is LTO8, because HP's own catalogue stops"
" at the Ultrium 8-SCSI. **sony-latest** is AIT4, not LTO at all. And "
"StorageTek has two, because an SL500 takes both its own T10000C and an "
"IBM LTO drive, so \"the latest cartridge\" has two answers and the file "
"gives both."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:110
#: 1b42ca40bb2740c8b3aa4213f325aef6
msgid "In the console"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:112
#: cca7289b035647b0b7c89d189e510bfd
msgid ""
"**Libraries → Create Library**, then a vendor. If any presets are defined"
" for it, they are listed above the form under **Saved configurations**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:115
#: de45c987905944a5ab2505d54371254b
msgid "Saved configurations, above the library form"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:119
#: 5124bfd0c8fe427a96a9c3b4971fa9ca
msgid ""
"Each card is one line folded - the name, and the same sentence ``mhvtl "
"preset list`` prints beside it. Open one and it shows the breakdown and "
"the two commands: the one that uses it, and the one that would rebuild "
"it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:123
#: 3e780afb94a84e878ba0312c1fd56143
msgid ""
"Clicking a name fills the form in below, and **every value can still be "
"changed before you press Create**. The one in use is marked on the card, "
"and there is a control below the list to leave it again. Choosing a "
"preset is a plain link, so nothing is written by looking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:129
#: 78ebc20d6c3c444c88dd20b5b02bfab1
msgid "Reading one"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:145
#: 20d6a013ac784c5585399f2d5887b706
msgid ""
"Two lines carry the point. **fixed here** is what the preset decides. "
"**left to IBM** is what it does not, and what the profile will therefore "
"choose - here the drive's firmware revision."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:149
#: 5117965a37dc414a8ff1ada649acc0bb
msgid ""
"**usable** is a separate question from **valid**. A preset that names no "
"vendor is perfectly legal and still cannot create anything, because there"
" is no catalogue to fill the gaps from."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:154
#: e73c702c6d054a86ba4c17928a91de4d
msgid "Building one up"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:156
#: a9660695758c42e382e60a155520ca05
msgid ""
"A preset does not have to be written in one go. ``preset set`` adds to or"
" changes one key at a time, and the keys are spelled exactly as the "
"command line's options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:169
#: 1a3959b0f71e440a90e7682245ecf135
msgid ""
"It says so rather than refusing. Half-built is a legal state, and "
"``preset list`` keeps saying which ones are in it, so a name is never a "
"trap:"
msgstr ""

