#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:199
#: faea2f82b5b4463a8550172c24b8a32a
msgid "Keeping one from a create that worked"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:201
#: 53c25c05160646dc9b73ec55a2487697
msgid ""
"The other way round, and usually the better one: build the library, see "
"that it works, *then* name the configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:210
#: 951880629a304866abd1740c175db640
msgid ""
"The preset is written from the specification that was just proved, so it "
"cannot disagree with the library you have."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:214
#: 786b1066ae5a4f16bde3509d3310b97a
msgid "An argument still beats the file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:216
#: 3bfbd20b139a437587f040e3a8545b05
msgid "A preset sets the defaults; the command line overrides them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:222
#: 58a9de0859a9436d91d42b4a272c8772
msgid ""
"That builds the preset's library with five cartridges instead of twenty, "
"and changes nothing in ``presets.toml``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:226
#: e357f232727242cc8538856599844ff8
msgid "What a preset will not let you do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:228
#: 67bf9f18af1f4a0aa04ddc7812c729e5
msgid ""
"It cannot hold a combination the vendor does not make. The check happens "
"when you save it, not when you finally try to use it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:238
#: 2670548071df47d3ba8a21ef5997dd93
msgid ""
"And it cannot take a profile's name, because that would make the two "
"words mean the same thing:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:249
#: 140b6510955248ea9cac35680297ce6e
msgid "Where they live"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:251
#: 5819c3badd4f4a81ba273edbfe7fdd57
msgid ""
"``/etc/mhvtl-gui/presets.toml``, written by the commands above and "
"readable by hand. The file is yours; the console only ever adds to it "
"what you asked for."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:255
#: 79c06609e3804f9ea75fd80ed2c802ba
msgid ""
"``/etc/mhvtl-gui/presets.toml.example`` beside it is the shipped set, and"
" **an upgrade replaces it** - so a preset written into the example file "
"would be lost. Copy what you want into ``presets.toml`` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:259
#: 50c1b2577aa14cceb89f933ced825c78
msgid ""
"Editing ``presets.toml`` by hand is supported and the keys are the "
"command line's, so a table reads as the command it replaces:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/profiles-and-presets.rst:273
#: 708e855f83bc4a6b89a2781bcca0af28
msgid ""
"Writing it needs the ``mhvtl`` group, like every other change the console"
" makes to the host - so the read verbs work as any user and the write "
"verbs want ``sudo``."
msgstr ""

